+  // no longer names an object of the type its dispatch header claims, or a
+  // caller asking for a type the header does not name. Both are rate-limited -
+  // the first is repaired (the structure is initialised again), the second is
+  // refused - and both mean the guest's structure and this SDK's object table
+  // have drifted apart, which is worth a line in the log but not a fault.
+  static void ReportNativeObjectAnomaly(const char* what, const void* native_ptr, int32_t as_type,
